   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 4.2. Strengthened capacity of enterprises to adopt new business models, technology and techniques to enhance productivity and sustainability</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Government of Solomon Islands introduced a new form of service provision for start ups using the ILO Start Your Business Programme in July 2021 and as a result 400 young people has undergone the ILO Start Your Business Programme in the rural sectors and have started community based micro enterprises. In Solomon Islands in partnership with the United Nations Development Programme and in  collaboration with the World Vision and Development Services Exchange, the ILO undertook the design of enterprise materials, delivery of Entrepreneurship trainings using ILO Start Your Business materials to 400 youths in the rural sector by support in the identification, design and implementation of new forms of community business. The partnership also included training of trainers to ten youths to become mentors on Social Entrepreneurship to support the community projects for sustainability. The ILO also conducted  a training course &quot;Youth takes the Floor&quot; on empowering youth as agents for peace and social cohesion in May 2021 in partnership with International Training Centre.</narrative>
